+## Other findings
+
+Genuine problems noticed while tracing verification (not verification gaps themselves):
+
+- **`pick_dst` allocates two fresh dynamic arrays per packet spawn from the run
+  arena** (`core/flow.odin:367-384`; `delete` is a no-op on an arena). Measured:
+  ~96 bytes/spawn, ~4.9 MB over a 3100-tick surge run against the 16 MB run arena
+  (`app/run/run.odin:52`). Bounded in practice because every run gets a fresh arena
+  (win/lose caps run length), but it contradicts the "zero per-frame heap churn" claim
+  and the margin is ~3 runs' worth, not infinite.
+- **`TICK_SECONDS :: 0.1`** (`app/run/run.odin:11`) is unused, with a comment claiming
+  it is "derived from balance.logic_hz" — it isn't; `driver.tick_seconds` is.
+- **`app.autopilot_wired`** (`app/main.odin:31, 152-155`) is written but never read —
+  the live map is `rc.autopilot_wired` (`app/run/autopilot.odin:14-17`).
+- **The §10.5 diff bundle is thinner than spec'd**: `diff.json` carries only
+  frame/pixel counts/bbox (`harness/goldens.odin:128-133`) — no `first_divergent_tick`,
+  no `event_stream_delta`, no `replay.dem`; reports overwrite a single `latest/`
+  directory instead of timestamped dirs.
+- **`load_catalogs` silently mixes disk and embedded bytes per file**
+  (`app/run/catalogs.odin:33-44`): a partially-populated `data/` dir yields a hybrid
+  catalog with no warning (the hash covers the hybrid, so goldens catch drift — but the
+  dev loop can silently test something other than either source).
+- **The catalog loader's claimed "unknown fields abort" validation doesn't exist**
+  (`core/catalog.odin:1-5` vs the lenient `jstr`/`jint` accessors); `jint` also
+  silently truncates `json.Float` values (`catalog.odin:351-357`) despite the
+  "no silent int truncation" narrative.
+- **`expect hash stable` is decorative** — T1 compare runs for every demo regardless
+  (`harness/main.odin:252-256`); harmless, but the directive's presence/absence means
+  nothing.
+- **Core tests leak-report** (arena/heap frees skipped in fixtures) — `odin test`
+  prints leak traces but exits 0; cosmetic today, noise that could hide a real
+  allocator regression tomorrow.
